Let me write the PreferenceSwitch component:

```vue
<template>
  <div class="pref-switch" :class="'pref-switch--' + variant">
    <span v-if="variant === 'drawer'" class="pref-switch__title">{{ $t('header.settings') }}</span>
    <div class="pref-switch__group">
      <span class="pref-switch__label">{{ $t('header.languageLabel') }}</span>
      <el-dropdown trigger="click" @command="handleLocale">
        <span class="pref-switch__btn">
          <i class="el-icon-... "></i>
          <span class="pref-switch__text">{{ localeLabel }}</span>
          <i class="el-icon-arrow-down pref-switch__caret"></i>
        </span>
        <el-dropdown-menu slot="dropdown">
          <el-dropdown-item v-for="opt in localeOptions" :key="opt.value" :command="opt.value" :class="{'is-current': localeSetting===opt.value}">
            {{ optionLabel(opt) }}
          </el-dropdown-item>
        </el-dropdown-menu>
      </el-dropdown>
    </div>
    ... theme group
  </div>
</template>
```

For the language icon: use a simple text badge "文/A"? I'll use `<i class="el-icon-...">`. Element doesn't have a globe. Options: use the Chinese character "文" styled as icon? I'd rather use a small inline SVG. Let me create a tiny inline SVG globe in the component template (no dependency):

```html
<svg class="pref-switch__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true">
  <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
  <ellipse cx="12" cy="12" rx="4" ry="9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
  <path d="M3.6 9h16.8M3.6 15h16.8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
</svg>
```
Good, self-contained.

Theme icon: `<i :class="themeIconClass">` where day → el-icon-sunny, night → el-icon-moon, auto → el-icon-moon-night (or a half sun/moon). Auto resolved theme determines icon per spec (sun/moon dual state): currentTheme (resolved) → sun/moon; if mode is auto, add a small "A" badge or use `el-icon-moon-night`? I'll show sun/moon based on the RESOLVED theme (so it reflects reality) and add a dot/badge when mode is auto, plus the dropdown shows the selected item. Simpler: icon = resolved theme (sunny/moon); add class `is-auto` to show a tiny "A" superscript. I'll show a small text label "自动"/"Auto" next to it when auto mode. Hmm, keep it clean:

- Bar variant: icon (sun/moon) + caret. Title attribute explains.
- Also add `.is-auto` marker: small dot.

I'll include a `title` attr with the mode label for accessibility.

Now the store: add themeMode + localeSetting state and mutations, and an `initPreferences` action? Keep simple:

```js
import { readThemeMode, setThemeMode as applyThemeMode } from "@/utils/theme";
import { readLocaleSetting, applyLocale } from "@/i18n";
```
Careful: circular imports? store imports i18n/index.js which imports Vue/VueI18n and terms — no import of store. Fine.

state: `themeMode: readThemeMode(), localeSetting: readLocaleSetting()`
mutations: 
```
SET_THEME_MODE(state, mode) { state.themeMode = normalizeThemeMode(mode); applyThemeMode(state.themeMode); }
SET_LOCALE(state, setting) { state.localeSetting = normalizeLocaleSetting(setting); applyLocale(state.localeSetting); }
```
actions: setThemeMode / setLocale dispatch commits.

Note: vuex-persistedstate `paths: ["breadcrumbListDetail"]` — only that path persisted, so these aren't persisted by vuex; the utils persist them. Good.

main.js: 
```js
import i18n, { initLocale } from "@/i18n";
import { initTheme } from "@/utils/theme";
import "./assets/css/theme.css";
```
Order: theme.css import after global.css and rich-content.css. But element-ui/bootstrap CSS are imported before. The theme.css must come after global.css → place its import right after rich-content.css import. And also `import App from "./App.vue"` is before; App.vue's style injection order in dev comes first (as discussed) → theme.css later wins. 

Also: `new Vue({ i18n, router, store, ... })`.

Also the ElementUI locale sync must happen before components render → call `initLocale()` before new Vue. And `initTheme()`.

Careful with import order for hoisting: `import i18n from "./i18n"` will execute the i18n module (creating VueI18n instance) at import time. `initLocale()` called later in module body. Also `Vue.use(ElementUI)` must run before `ElementLocale.use()`? ElementLocale.use just sets a locale object — independent of Vue.use. But `Vue.use(ElementUI, { i18n })` — ElementUI's `install` accepts `i18n` option for `t` function; the default ElementUI locale is zh-CN when no lang specified. To make ElementUI fully switch, `ElementLocale.use(lang)` works after Vue.use(ElementUI). Our initLocale() runs after all imports (imports hoisted, so Vue.use(ElementUI) at line 26 executes before body statements). Since `initLocale()` is called in the body (after imports), ordering is fine.

Also, main.js currently calls `Vue.use(BaiduMap, ...)` at the bottom — fine.

public/index.html: add inline pre-boot script to set data-theme + a background color so there's no white flash before the bundle runs. It must replicate the token values minimally:

```html
<script>
  (function () {
    var d = document.documentElement;
    var mode = "auto";
    try { var s = localStorage.getItem("aska-theme"); if (s === "day" || s === "night" || s === "auto") mode = s; } catch (e) {}
    var theme = mode === "auto"
      ? (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "night" : "day")
      : mode;
    d.setAttribute("data-theme", theme);
    d.setAttribute("data-theme-mode", mode);
    d.style.colorScheme = theme === "night" ? "dark" : "light";
    d.style.backgroundColor = theme === "night" ? "#0B1A2F" : "#D6E8F5";
  })();
  (function () {
    var lang = null;
    try { lang = localStorage.getItem("aska-locale"); } catch (e) {}
    if (lang !== "zh-CN" && lang !== "en-US") {
      var nav = (navigator.languages && navigator.languages[0]) || navigator.language || "";
      lang = /^zh/i.test(nav) ? "zh-CN" : "en";
    }
    document.documentElement.setAttribute("lang", lang);
  })();
</script>
```

Also update `<html lang="zh-CN">`? Leave as "" and let the script set it. Also update the noscript text and title? Title is `askatek.cn` — fine.

Now HeaderContent: add the PreferenceSwitch into `.header-btn` (bar variant, desktop only) and into the drawer (drawer variant). Also translate nav titles and search placeholder.

