content.text:
Issue: `initLocale()` is called at line 30, before `Vue.use(ElementUI)` at 33. applyLocale calls `ElementLocale.use(elementZhCN)` — that sets element-ui's locale module state; `Vue.use(ElementUI)` later doesn't reset it (ElementUI's install uses `locale.use`? Actually element-ui's install does: `Vue.prototype.$ELEMENT = { size, zIndex }` and if `opts.i18n` provided uses it. The default `locale` used by components comes from `element-ui/lib/locale/index.js`'s `use()` which sets `lang` and `i18n`. Hmm, in element-ui's locale module:

```js
export default {
  install(Vue) {...},
  use(lang) { lang && (this.lang = lang); ... }
}
```
Wait, actually element-ui/lib/locale/index.js:
```js
import defaultLang from 'element-ui/lib/locale/lang/zh-CN';
import Vue from 'vue';
import Format from './format';
const format = Format(Vue);
let lang = defaultLang;
let merged = false;
let i18nHandler = function() {...};
export const t = function(path, options) {...};
export default {
  use(lang) {...},
  t,
  i18n(fn) {...}
};
```
And `element-ui/lib/locale/index.js` exports `use` — yes, `ElementLocale.use(lang)` is the documented API. It requires Vue to be set? `Format(Vue)` uses Vue.util.warn. Fine.

But to be safe, move initLocale()/initTheme() after `Vue.use(ElementUI)` and before `new Vue`. Theme must be applied ASAP for FOUC, but the inline script in index.html handles the first paint; initTheme in JS just syncs. I'll place both after the Vue.use block.

Also ElementUI's `Vue.use(ElementUI)` without i18n option uses the module-level lang — so calling ElementLocale.use after is fine too. Order: Vue.use(ElementUI) then initLocale().

Let me restructure: keep `initTheme()` early (line 29) and put `initLocale()` after Vue.use(ElementUI). Add i18n to the Vue instance.

Also need `Vue.use(preview)` — commented out, irrelevant.

Edit main.js accordingly.

