Now let me verify the dev server still works after the npm reshuffle (it recompiled on my edits — HMR). Let me write the puppeteer script for interactive verification:

1. Launch Edge headless via puppeteer-core with executablePath.
2. Open http://127.0.0.1:8081/shunkai-dg/#/ (no query params → default auto/system; but headless Chrome defaults to light color scheme, so auto → day).
3. Verify:
   - `document.documentElement.dataset.theme` = 'day'
   - locale: system is likely en-US → nav "About aska". Then click the language dropdown and select 中文 → check nav text becomes 关于 aska and `html lang="zh-CN"` and localStorage `aska-locale` = 'zh-CN'.
   - Click the theme dropdown → choose 黑夜 (or Night) → check `data-theme='night'`, `.theme-transition` class was added during transition, and `localStorage['aska-theme']='night'`.
   - Then switch to 跟随系统 / Follow system → check `data-theme-mode='auto'`.
   - Screenshot each state.
   - Also open the mobile drawer (viewport 420x900), click the hamburger (`.list-ul img`), screenshot the drawer with the pref switch row.
   - Also test the Product Center hover panel (subNav) in night mode for contrast.
   - Also test the footer in night mode (scroll to bottom).
   - Check computed styles: body bg in day = rgb(214,232,245), night = rgb(11,26,47); text color; header bg.

Let me write this as a Node script file in .shots/ (outside src, e.g. `D:\ZZH\aska\github\shunkai-dg\.verify\check.js`) and run it with node. Wait — the sandbox note says Node child_process with piped stdio fails under confinement, but we're in danger-full-access now. Running `node script.js` directly from pwsh is fine.

Let me write the script. Keep it robust: wait for selectors, use page.click with text selectors via XPath or el-dropdown-item classes.

ElementUI dropdown: items render in `.el-dropdown-menu__item` appended to body. So: click `.pref-switch__item:first-child .pref-switch__trigger`, wait for `.el-dropdown-menu:not([style*="display: none"])`, then click the item with text.

Simpler: use page.evaluate to find and click elements by text content.

Let me write:

```js
const puppeteer = require('puppeteer-core');
const EDGE = 'C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft\\Edge\\Application\\msedge.exe';
const BASE = 'http://127.0.0.1:8081/shunkai-dg/';
const OUT = 'D:\\ZZH\\aska\\github\\shunkai-dg\\.shots\\';

const sleep = (ms) => new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, ms));

async function clickByText(page, selector, text) {
  const ok = await page.evaluate((sel, txt) => {
    const els = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll(sel));
    const hit = els.find(e => (e.textContent || '').trim().includes(txt));
    if (hit) { hit.click(); return true; }
    return false;
  }, selector, text);
  if (!ok) throw new Error(`not found: ${selector} containing "${text}"`);
}

(async () => {
  const browser = await puppeteer.launch({ executablePath: EDGE, headless: 'new', args: ['--no-first-run','--no-default-browser-check','--disable-gpu'], defaultViewport: { width: 1440, height: 900 } });
  const page = await browser.newPage();
  const results = [];
  const log = (k, v) => { results.push([k, v]); console.log(k + ': ' + JSON.stringify(v)); };

  await page.goto(BASE, { waitUntil: 'networkidle2' });
  await sleep(1200);
  log('initial theme attr', await page.evaluate(() => document.documentElement.getAttribute('data-theme')));
  log('initial mode attr', await page.evaluate(() => document.documentElement.getAttribute('data-theme-mode')));
  log('initial lang attr', await page.evaluate(() => document.documentElement.getAttribute('lang')));
  log('body bg', await page.evaluate(() => getComputedStyle(document.body).backgroundColor));
  log('header bg', await page.evaluate(() => getComputedStyle(document.querySelector('.askatek-header')).backgroundColor));
  log('nav texts', await page.evaluate(() => Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.el-menu--horizontal .el-menu-item, .el-menu--horizontal .el-submenu__title')).map(e => e.textContent.trim())));

  // 语言切到中文
  await page.click('.pref-switch__item:nth-child(2) .pref-switch__trigger');  // careful: heading span may be first child in drawer only
  ...
```
Hmm, `.pref-switch__item` is the el-dropdown root element; in the bar variant the children are: el-dropdown (item) ×2. So `.pref-switch__item` nth-of-type(1) = language, (2) = theme. In the drawer variant there's a heading span (not .pref-switch__item) so nth-of-type still works? `:nth-child(2)` counts all children including the heading span. Use `page.$$('.pref-switch__item')` and index [0], [1] instead — robust.

Then click the item: after opening, `.el-dropdown-menu__item` elements appear in the popper. Use clickByText(page, '.el-dropdown-menu__item', '中文').

Careful: two dropdown menus exist after opening (one for lang, one for theme) — only the opened one is visible. Use `document.querySelectorAll('.el-dropdown-menu__item')` filtered by visibility (offsetParent !== null).

Let me write the script with a helper that clicks only visible elements.

Steps & assertions:
1. initial state (auto/auto).
2. language dropdown → 中文 → nav Chinese, html lang zh-CN, localStorage aska-locale = zh-CN.
3. theme dropdown → 黑夜 → theme night, html data-theme night, bg check, transition class present right after click.
4. screenshot night (top of page), then scroll to footer & screenshot, hover Product Center nav item → screenshot subNav.
5. theme → 跟随系统 (auto in Chinese: "跟随系统") → mode auto; since headless defaults to light → theme day.
6. language → English → nav English; then language → 跟随系统 → label shows Follow system.
7. Check the burger drawer at 420x900: click `.list-ul img`, screenshot the drawer.
8. Report transition class during switch: after clicking night, immediately evaluate `document.documentElement.classList.contains('theme-transition')`.

Also verify prefers-color-scheme emulation: `page.emulateMediaFeatures([{name:'prefers-color-scheme', value:'dark'}])` then re-check that auto mode → night. That's a great test of "随系统切换"! Do it: set auto + emulate dark → data-theme should become night without interaction (media query listener).

Let me write and run it.

