The lang trigger title is "语言: 跟随系统" — because in auto mode `localeLabel` returns `$t('common.theme.auto')` = "跟随系统" (a small bug: it should use `common.lang.auto`, same text in this case, fine) — and my assertion required it to also contain "English|中文". The UI shows "跟随系统" for auto mode, which is correct-ish, but it doesn't tell the user which system language is being followed.

Improvement: in auto mode, the trigger should show the *resolved* language, e.g. "中文（跟随系统）" / "English (Follow system)". That's better UX and satisfies the spec's "随系统设置". Let me update PreferenceSwitch.localeLabel:

```js
localeLabel() {
  const active = this.activeLocale === LOCALE_ZH ? this.$t("common.lang.zh") : this.$t("common.lang.en");
  if (this.localeSetting === LOCALE_AUTO) {
    return active + " · " + this.$t("common.lang.auto");  // 中文 · 跟随系统
  }
  return active;
}
```
Hmm, in the bar variant the text isn't shown (icon only), only the title. So this affects the drawer + title. "中文 · 跟随系统" is a bit long but informative. Let me use that.

Also in the drawer variant the same label is shown — good.

Then update the assertion: title should contain the resolved language AND (for auto) the system note. Let me simply assert /(中文|English)/ and /(Language|语言)/.

Let me apply both changes and re-run.

